@startuml sequence_diagram_gui

title GUI User Interaction: Calculation with Service Delegation

actor User
participant GUIApplication as GUI
participant CalculatorService as Service
participant InterfaceLayer as Interface
participant CalculationLayer as CalcLayer
participant MemoryStore as MemStore

User -> GUI: Click "+" button (Add operation)
activate GUI

User -> GUI: Enter operands, click "="
activate GUI

GUI -> Service: perform(add, 5, 3)
activate Service

Service -> Interface: perform(add, 5, 3)
activate Interface

' Calculate phase
Interface -> CalcLayer: perform_calculation(add, 5, 3)
activate CalcLayer
CalcLayer --> Interface: return CalculationResult(add, [5,3], 8.0)
deactivate CalcLayer

' Store phase (automatic in perform_with_memory)
Interface -> MemStore: store(ResultEntry)
activate MemStore
MemStore --> Interface: return
deactivate MemStore

Interface --> Service: return CalculationResult
deactivate Interface

Service --> GUI: return 8.0
deactivate Service

GUI -> GUI: display_var.set("8.0")
GUI --> User: Show result in display
deactivate GUI

User -> GUI: Click History Tab
activate GUI

GUI -> MemStore: retrieve()
activate MemStore
MemStore --> GUI: list[MemoryEntry]
deactivate MemStore

GUI -> GUI: _refresh_history()
GUI -> GUI: Populate listbox with formatted entries
GUI --> User: Display history with error highlighting
deactivate GUI

note right of GUI
  **GUIApplication:**
  - No business logic
  - No calculation code
  - Pure presentation layer
  - Delegates to CalculatorService
  - Accesses MemoryStore for history
end note

note right of Service
  **CalculatorService:**
  - Orchestrates InterfaceLayer
  - All results persist to storage
  - No GUI-specific code
end note

@enduml
